-- ============================================================
-- Import: existing BGL customers (from Customer_Listing-10-Jul-2026.xlsx)
-- ============================================================
-- Generated from the spreadsheet provided on 10 Sept 2026 -- 558
-- customer records, opened outside this system. Run once against
-- the same Supabase project, after migration_existing_customers.sql.
--
-- NOT safe to blindly re-run as-is: running this twice would insert
-- every row a second time (no unique constraint prevents it, since
-- Cust_ID / CHN / CSCS aren't guaranteed unique in the source data
-- and email has many legitimate duplicates -- see below). If you
-- need to re-import an updated list, clear the table first:
--   truncate table existing_bgl_customers;
-- then re-run this file.
--
-- Data quality notes from the source file, so nothing here is a
-- surprise: 20 of 558 rows have no email at all (can't be matched
-- against on account opening -- included anyway for completeness of
-- the customer record); many rows share the same email across
-- multiple rows (joint holders / related accounts under one contact
-- email is common in the source data) -- this is expected and fine
-- for the duplicate-check use case, since the check only needs to
-- know an email exists at all, not that it's unique.







